WEBVTT

00:00:15.723 --> 00:00:18.559
I can't believe we got double-crossed
by a tiny rodent.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:21.228
Oh, we got double-crossed
by a rodent, all right.

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:23.230
But, uh, not a tiny one.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:24.398
What?

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:27.317
This was supposed to be
us conning Marmalade.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:30.320
It turns out, it was Wolf conning us.

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:32.197
[gagging]

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:35.450
- Does that sound familiar to you, Wolf?
- Why would you think that?

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.203
I don't know,
maybe because you just sabotaged

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:40.414
the biggest heist of our lives?

00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:42.791
I think you owe us
an explanation, buddy.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:45.043
[sighs]

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.670
Okay. You're right.

00:00:46.754 --> 00:00:47.838
This is what happened.

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:51.341
Back in the museum,
I just tried to steal an old lady's purse.

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:52.676
Classic snatch and grab.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.303
"Tried to"?

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:57.097
Since when do you try to steal something
and not just steal it?

00:00:57.181 --> 00:01:00.559
I was trying to steal the purse,
when the old lady fell...

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:02.436
[clears throat]
...and I kinda helped her.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.478
What?

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.606
I kinda helped her.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.898
But then you stole her purse?

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.734
No. I didn't.

00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:13.030
I saved the old lady, and she hugged me,
and my tail wagged,

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:16.074
and I didn't know what it was,
but it felt, you know...

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:17.701
good.

00:01:17.785 --> 00:01:19.286
[all gasp]

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.247
Ah! But then,
you stole the purse?

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:23.957
[all] No!

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:27.711
You know, I heard what the pig said
to you about cuttin' us loose.

00:01:27.795 --> 00:01:30.047
Wait. Like, "us" us?

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:32.341
But I never thought
you'd actually do it, man.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.550
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:36.094
I would never... I was tryin' to...

00:01:36.179 --> 00:01:38.180
I was trying to find us a better life.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.975
Our life was perfect
until you decided to ruin it.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.060
[Wolf] I didn't.

00:01:43.144 --> 00:01:45.354
You guys felt it at the gala.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.397
The clapping, the cheering.

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:50.275
We were more than just scary villains.
They loved us.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.944
Oh, yeah? If they loved us so much,

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:56.031
how come we're in prison
for a crime we didn't commit?

00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:57.658
You know what?

00:01:57.742 --> 00:02:01.244
I'll give Marmalade this:
At least he sees the world for what it is:

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:05.332
A place where some people are scary
and some people are scared.

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:08.835
Oh, yeah? Well, I'm tired of bein' scary.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.837
I'm tired of bein' an outcast.

00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:13.298
- Maybe I don't wanna be a...
- What? A bad guy?

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:15.717
Don't wanna be
a bad guy anymore, huh?

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.968
Say it, Wolf!

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:21.139
Yeah, I thought so.

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:23.684
And us? Your lifelong friends?

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:24.893
We're just holdin' you back?

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.645
Yeah, maybe you are!

00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:29.106
[gasps]

00:02:30.608 --> 00:02:31.775
- Take it back.
- Snake!

00:02:31.859 --> 00:02:33.527
Take it back! Apologize!

00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:35.487
Hey, hey, hey!

00:02:35.571 --> 00:02:37.322
Prison is no place for fighting.

00:02:38.741 --> 00:02:40.075
Tell that to him.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.159
[Wolf] Huh?

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:48.208
- What?
- [shouting]

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.591
[grunts, shouts]

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.676
[shouts]

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.764
[high-pitched shout, screams]

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.851
- [guard screaming]
- Shh.

00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:13.817
[shouts]

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:20.031
[screams]

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.875
[both grunt]

00:03:31.335 --> 00:03:32.711
Wait, wait! Hold...

00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:36.214
[all gasp] Diane?

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:38.717
But how do you know how to do
all of that kick-kick-punch-punch?

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:41.219
Wait a sec, you're the Crimson Paw?

00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:46.516
<i>[Wolf] The Queen of Cons,</i>
<i>Acrobatic Swiss Army Knife,</i>

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.102
<i>stole the Zumpango diamond twice,</i>
<i>once for profit,</i>

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:50.729
<i>second time just for fun.</i>

00:03:50.813 --> 00:03:53.440
<i>Never identified, never caught.</i>

00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:57.569
[chuckles] Guess I'm still the best
bad guy the world has ever seen.

00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:00.781
- [sighs] At least I used to be.
- [alarm blaring]

00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:02.741
- [guards screaming]
- [Wolf, Shark gasp]

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:07.662
[screams]

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.168
Nope, I am still the best.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.629
Just like riding a stolen bicycle.

00:04:16.214 --> 00:04:18.340
Oh. Uh, you got a little... Ouch.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.675
Hey, why...
Why did you save us anyway?

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.053
After the gala,
I knew something wasn't right.

00:04:23.137 --> 00:04:25.055
So, I did some investigating,
and that meteor...

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:26.139
I know.

00:04:26.224 --> 00:04:28.892
Some kinda
cosmic-mega-super-antennae thing.

00:04:28.976 --> 00:04:31.520
Right. If conducted through
an array of ionized crystals,

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.981
it will generate a massive
psychokinetic field the size of a city.

00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:37.651
Oh, my gosh, did I interrupt you?
Were you gonna say that?

00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:41.613
Uh... I was gonna be a little more
technical, but you got the gist of it.

00:04:41.697 --> 00:04:42.739
[Diane laughs]

00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:47.577
Marmalade needs to be stopped,
but I can't do it alone.

00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:51.164
- You know his compound better than anyone.
- You can count on us.

00:04:51.249 --> 00:04:52.541
Right, guys?

00:04:53.376 --> 00:04:54.876
There is no "us."

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.503
We're through, Wolf.

00:04:56.587 --> 00:04:58.421
Done. Finito.

00:04:58.506 --> 00:05:00.215
Because of that little tiff back there?

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:03.051
Come on, man, that's what we do.

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:05.220
You serve, I volley.
That's our little dance.

00:05:06.514 --> 00:05:07.848
Not this time.

00:05:13.396 --> 00:05:14.396
Piranha?

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.359
Webs?

00:05:19.443 --> 00:05:20.735
Sorry, Wolfie.

00:05:22.864 --> 00:05:24.030
Shark...

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:25.574
Hmm.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:26.825
Hey.

00:05:27.743 --> 00:05:28.743
Guys?

00:05:29.912 --> 00:05:31.204
Guys?

00:05:32.373 --> 00:05:34.499
You wanna know why I hate birthdays, Wolf?

00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:35.458
Do you?

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:41.047
When you grow up a snake,
nobody shows up to your party.

00:05:41.132 --> 00:05:44.175
Birthdays are a constant reminder
that out there

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:48.805
I'm just a scary,
good-for-nothin' monster.

00:05:50.433 --> 00:05:51.474
Yeah.

00:05:52.435 --> 00:05:55.186
But nothing compares
to havin' the one guy...

00:05:55.271 --> 00:05:58.565
The one guy I thought I could trust...

00:05:59.108 --> 00:06:00.400
Stab me in the back.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.615
Come on, guys. Let's get outta here.

